================================
# QUESTION : TIMEOUT KYA HAI ?
================================

Timeout ek maximum time limit hai jo caller side set karta hai 
— client, service, load balancer, API gateway, ya database client.

Agar is time limit ke andar target system se 
koi bhi response nahi aata — na success, na failure —
to caller wait karna band kar deta hai 
aur us request ko apni side se failed maan leta hai.


## IMPORTANT :
---------------

Timeout hone ka matlab ye nahi ki target system ne request process nahi ki.
Timeout hone ke baad bhi ye possibility hoti hai ki target system ne request process kar li ho, 
lekin response na de paaya ho — network issue, response bhejte waqt crash etc.
Isliye Non-idempotent operations me timeout ke baad blindly retry nahi karte
Production-grade systems me operations ko idempotent banate hain.



## QUESTION : TIMEOUT KYUN ZAROORI HAI ?
------------------------------------------

Har incoming request ko process karne ke liye ek worker thread allocate hota hai (jaise Tomcat me).
Maan lo ek worker thread ne kisi external API ko call kiya — jaise Payment Service, DB, ya koi downstream service.
Agar us API call ke liye koi timeout configured nahi hai, aur target system se response hi nahi aa raha (slow, hung, ya network issue),
to ye worker thread indefinitely block reh jayegi. Ab isi tarah aur requests aati hain, aur har ek apna worker thread block kar leti hai.
Jaise-jaise aisi requests aati hain, thread pool ke threads khatam hone lagte hain. Jaise hi saare worker threads block ho jaate hain — jaise Tomcat me default 200 threads hote hain, 
ya kisi bhi configured thread pool size tak — thread pool exhaust ho jaata hai.  Uske baad nayi requests ke paas process hone ke liye koi free thread nahi bachta.
Wo ya to queue me wait karti hain, ya reject ho jaati hain.

Thread pool exhaustion ki wajah se:

### 1. BAD USER EXPERIENCE
-----------------------------
User ko slow response milta hai ya UI par infinite spinner dikhta hai — jaise "your request is being processed". 
Infinite spinner dikhane se better hai fast error dena. User ko jaldi pata chalta hai ki kuch galat hua.


### 2. RESOURCE BLOCKED
--------------------------
Blocked thread apne saath kai system resources (jaise memory, connection) hold karke rakhti hai. 
Timeout ke baad ye sab free ho jaate hain.


### 3. FAILURE DETECTION DIFFICULT
------------------------------------
Bina timeout ke koi exception throw nahi hoti, request bas hang reh jaati hai aur thread block ho jaata hai, lekin logs me koi error entry nahi aati, isliye problem chhupi rehti hai; 
aur koi clear signal na hone ki wajah se root cause locate karna bhi mushkil ho jaata hai — pata nahi chalta kaunsi dependency (Payment Service, DB, downstream) slow hai,
jisse debugging manual ho jaati hai aur thread dump lena padta hai.


### 4. CASCADING FAILURE
---------------------------
Cascading Failure tab hota hai jab ek service slow ya fail hoti hai, aur ye failure upstream chain me propagate hoti jaati 
hai — ek ke baad ek service fail hone lagti hai, aur eventually poora system down ho jaata hai.

Example:

Client → Service A → Service B → Service C

Maan lo har service me 10 threads hain.

- Client ne 10 requests bheji → Service A ke 10 threads busy (Service B ka wait)
- Service B ke 10 threads busy (Service C ka wait)
- Service C slow ho gayi → Service B ke saare 10 threads block
- Service B blocked → Service A ke saare 10 threads bhi block
- Ab 11th request aayi → Service A ke paas free thread nahi → fail

Poora system hang

Failure neeche se upar cascade hui — isliye naam Cascading Failure.



## QUESTION : TIMEOUT KE TYPES ?
----------------------------------

1. CONNECTION TIMEOUT
-----------------------

- Client aur Server ke beech TCP connection establish hone mein agar specified time se zyada lag jaye, toh Connection Timeout hota hai.
- Client ne SYN bheja, lekin SYN-ACK nahi aaya — could be server down, network issue, ya firewall ne silently drop kar diya. 
  Is wajah se TCP connection establish nahi hoti.
- Iska matlab hai request target tak pahunchi hi nahi, isliye safe to retry. 
- Typical value 1–3 seconds hoti hai. 
- Error: ConnectTimeoutException


### NOTE - CONNECTION REFUSED
------------------------------

- Connection Refused technically timeout nahi hai, lekin ye TCP connection phase me hota hai — isliye commonly Connection Timeout ke saath discuss karte hain. 
  Isme server reachable tha (network level pe), lekin us particular port pe koi service listen nahi kar rahi thi, isliye server ne turant RST (Reset) packet bhej
  diya aur connection immediately fail ho gaya — koi wait nahi hua.
- Connection Timeout se main farak ye hai ki timeout me response hi nahi aata (caller ko wait karna padta hai, phir fail hota hai), 
  jabki Connection Refused me RST turant aata hai (fast fail, no waiting).
- Common reasons: galat port number, service crash ho gayi ho, ya firewall actively connection reject kar raha ho. 


2. WRITE TIMEOUT 
-----------------

- Write Timeout tab hota hai jab client aur server ke beech TCP 3-way handshake complete ho jaata hai, 
  TCP connection establish ho jaata hai. Agar HTTPS request bhejna hai to uske liye TLS handshake complete 
  bhi karna padta hai. TLS handshake successfully complete hone ke baad encrypted channel establish ho jaata hai, 
  aur client HTTP/ HTTPS request bhejna shuru karta hai — yaani write() call karta hai.
  Agar ye write operation specified time ke andar complete nahi hota, to Write Timeout trigger hota hai.
- Ye mostly tab hota hai jab payload bada ho — jaise file upload. Buffer full ho jaata hai aur write() call multiple 
  chunks me data bhejta hai. Agar network slow ya server slow hai, to write() block ho jaata hai aur write timeout trigger hota hai.
- Write timeout ke baad result indeterminate hota hai — request server tak pahunchi hi nahi, partially pahunchi, ya poori pahunch gayi
  lekin client ko last data segment ka ACK nahi mila. Isliye non-idempotent operations me blindly retry nahi karte
- Typical value usually Read Timeout ke barabar ya thoda kam.




3. READ TIMEOUT (Socket Timeout)
-----------------------------------

- Read Timeout tab hota hai jab client aur server ke beech TCP 3-way handshake complete ho jaata hai, 
  aur TCP connection establish ho jaata hai. Agar HTTPS request bhejni hai, to uske liye TLS handshake 
  complete karna padta hai. TLS handshake successfully complete hone ke baad encrypted channel establish ho jaata hai.
  Ab client HTTP/HTTPS request bhejta hai — yaani request server tak pahunch jaati hai.
  Uske baad client response ka wait karta hai. Agar is response wait me specified time se zyada lag jaye,
  to Read Timeout trigger hota hai.
- Read timeout ke baad result indeterminate hota hai — request server tak pahunch chuki thi, aur process bhi ho chuki ho 
  sakti hai. Sirf response nahi aaya. Isliye non-idempotent operations me blindly retry nahi karte .
- Common reasons: Server slow, DB slow, Downstream service slow, Deadlock
- Typical value 1–3 seconds hoti hai. 
- Error: SocketTimeoutException



4. REQUEST TIMEOUT
--------------------

- Total Request Timeout ek maximum allowed time hai jo ek poori request ko complete hone ke liye diya jaata hai.
  Ye ek upper bound budget hai — isme sab kuch cover hota hai:

  a) TCP connection establish karna (via TCP 3-way handshake)
  b) TLS handshake karna (agar HTTPS request bhejni hai)
  c) HTTP / HTTPS Request write karna
  d) Response receive karna
  e) Retries (agar request fail hui to)
  f) Backoff delays (retries ke beech ka wait)

- Total Request Timeout ki value teen cheezon ke basis par decide karte hain:

  a) BUSINESS SLA KE BASIS PAR
     > Business ne kaha: "Payment API ka response 3 second me aana chahiye." → Total Timeout = 3s.
     > SLA se bada nahi rakh sakte. Warna SLA violate hoga — customer penalize karega, compliance issue aayega, regulatory audit me red flag.

  b) P99 LATENCY KE BASIS PAR
     > P99 = 100 requests me se 99 requests is time ke andar complete ho jaati hain. Sirf 1 request isse slow hoti hai.
     > Yaani P99 = 800ms ka matlab: 99% requests 800ms ya us se kam me complete hoti hain.
     > Total Request Timeout kabhi bhi P99 se kam nahi rakh sakte — warna legitimate slow requests bhi fail ho jaayengi
     > Right value: P99 + thoda buffer ≈ 1.5–2x P99

  c) RETRY BUDGET
    > Jin bhi timeouts par tumne retries configure kiye, unke total cumulative time se kam nahi rakh sakte Request Timeout ki value.
    > Agar 3 retries hain aur har attempt me ~1s lagta hai → Total Timeout kam se kam 3–4s hona chahiye — warna retries beech me hi cut ho jaayengi.

-  Conflict hone par SLA jeetta hai. Chahe P99 1s ho, chahe retry budget 4s ho — agar SLA 3s hai to Total Timeout 3s hi rahega.



5. SESSION TIMEOUT
--------------------

- Agar application HttpSession use kar rahi hai authentication/authorization ke liye, to hum define kar sakte hain ki wo HttpSession kitni der tak valid rahegi.
  Configured timeout tak user koi request nahi bhejta, to Tomcat automatically HttpSession destroy kar deta hai — user ko dobara login karna padta hai.
- Session timeout inactivity-based hota hai. Har request par timer reset hota hai. User active rahe to session expire nahi hogi.
- Typical value: 30 min (HttpSession ka default)
- Configure kaise (Spring Boot):
  server.servlet.session.timeout=30m     ← Single server + Distributed dono me kaam karta hai
  spring.session.timeout=30m             ← Optional; Spring Session specific override



6. CONNECTION POOL BORROW TIMEOUT 
-----------------------------------

- Connection Pool Borrow Timeout ek maximum wait time hai jo ek application thread (Tomcat worker thread) 
  apne database connection pool se connection borrow karne ke liye wait kar sakti hai.
- Error: Connection is not available, request timed out after Xms



## IMPORTANT
-------------
Jab ek request user se lekar database tak jaati hai, to wo multiple components se pass hoti hai. Har component ek "layer" hai, 
aur har layer apna timeout rakhti hai. Rule ek hi hai: outer layer ka timeout inner se bada rakho. Warna outer pehle fail karega, 
inner abhi bhi kaam karta rahega — resource waste.





